# AGENTS.md Template — Store Deployment Pointer

> Copy this section into your project's AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, or .cursorrules
> so any AI agent knows where to find deployment credentials and commands.

## 0. Store Deployment (Read First)

**All store deployment credentials and commands live in one place:**
→ [`docs/STORE_DEPLOYMENT.md`](docs/STORE_DEPLOYMENT.md)

This file contains:
- App Store Connect API key path, issuer ID, team ID
- Google Play service account JSON path, package name
- Build commands (AAB + IPA)
- Upload commands (`xcrun altool` + `fastlane supply`)
- Version bump protocol
- Full copy-paste release flow

**Any agent deploying to stores should read that file first.**
Do not search for credentials across the filesystem — they are
already documented there.

## Quick deploy

To deploy a new version:
1. Bump version in `pubspec.yaml`
2. Tell the agent: "Ship version X.Y.Z to both stores"
3. The agent reads `docs/STORE_DEPLOYMENT.md` and executes the full flow

## Blog/web deployment (if applicable)

If your blog/site auto-deploys on git push:
```bash
git add your-blog-dir/
git commit -m "blog: description"
git push origin main
# Your hosting platform (Render, Vercel, Netlify) auto-deploys
```
